                <pb facs="0406" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg307"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.689 Entry, Residence and Establishment/6:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Greece</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-09-25T18:00:00-04:00">September 25, 1936—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. Your 96, September 24, noon. Department relies upon Legation to assure that
                    Greek and English texts will be exactly identic in meaning. Full powers being
                    forwarded.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For text of treaty, signed at Athens, November 21, 1936, see Department of
                        State Treaty Series No. 930, or 51 Stat. 230.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
